      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "**Draft.** Defines what generated artifacts may be tracked in Rig Relay.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Core Rule",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Tracked source should stay small, durable, and reviewable. Generated runtime artifacts belong in `.build/` or another explicit runtime root unless a file is deliberately curated as a fixture or proof.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Do Not Track",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Session logs - Coordination state - Telemetry bundles - Chat transcripts - Desktop projections - Validation outputs - Derived evaluation dumps - Upload payloads - Temporary demo outputs - Raw evidence snapshots",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Track Only When Curated",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Minimal fixtures needed for tests - Hand-authored docs and policies - Schemas - Explicit demo assets - Proof artifacts that are documented as part of the release workflow",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-10",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Alpha Policy",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Keep `.build/` out of source control unless a specific file is intentionally curated - Do not expand tracked generated artifacts during alpha stabilization - Prefer regeneration over versioning for runtime outputs - Keep release commits focused on source, docs, schemas, and tests",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Validation",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Review `git status` before commit - Confirm generated artifacts are not being staged unintentionally - Keep public-facing docs content-light and free of raw evidence",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    }
  ],
